            <ArticleTitle>A young woman with myalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>525-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7861/clinmedicine.14-5-525</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the case of a young female presenting with myalgia, mildly raised creatine kinase and a rash. The discussion emphasises the importance of a systematic approach to muscle symptoms, the value of a detailed hand examination and the importance of magnetic resonance imaging in the investigation of muscular symptoms.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2014 Royal College of Physicians.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
